# .publish-allow — the binary files this repository may carry, by class.
#
# The pre-commit hook refuses any staged binary (git's own text/binary
# heuristic) whose path matches none of these globs, and the publish scan
# checks every tracked binary the same way. Being on this list is a decision
# that the class is OUR output, not the game's: screenshots of our renderer,
# figures we generated, models we trained, meshes we built. Files of the
# original game are refused by content hash regardless of this list
# (CLAUDE.md, "Publishing").
#
# One glob per line, matched against the repo-relative path; `*` crosses
# directory separators. Comments and blank lines are ignored.

# Notes: screenshots of our renderer and the figures the wiki pages embed
research/notes/assets/*

# Undither tool: screenshots of the app itself
tools/undither/screens/*.png

# Learned undither restorer: models we trained on a CC0 texture corpus
unditherer/models/*

# Replacement unit models we built (posed by the unit's own COB at runtime)
units/*.glb

# Impure's own UI art, drawn for Impure in each style's look and checked against the
# game's UI art by tools/artcheck.py; baked into the DLL by tools/artbake.py
art/ui/*

# The replay HUD's painted parts, lossless: painted for Impure from our whiteboxes and cut by
# tools/hudart/ (research/notes/hud-art.md); the mockup draws them, the DLL is to bake them
art/hud/*

# The same parts at the resolution they were cut at, which tools/hudart/fit.py fits into art/hud/
art/hud-full/*

# The in-game wiki's painted parts, lossless: painted for Impure in the replay HUD's look and cut by
# tools/hudart/ (research/notes/ingame-wiki.md, The art); the wiki mockup draws them and the DLL embeds
# them, fitted by tools/hudart/fit.py --set wiki
art/wiki/kit/*

# The same parts at the resolution they were cut at, which tools/hudart/fit.py fits into art/wiki/kit/
art/wiki-full/*

# NOT OUR OUTPUT: a mod's own art for its showcase on the Mods screen -- its logo, a banner, a backdrop --
# carried with the authors' permission its catalog entry records (mods/<id>.json `permission`), filed by
# the mod's id. tools/mods/genparts.py copies each into the wiki's kit as the part logo_<id>, banner_<id>
# or backdrop_<id> (art/wiki/kit/ above), which the DLL embeds; nothing of it is fetched from the web.
art/mods/logos/*
art/mods/banners/*
art/mods/backdrops/*

# The exe patch pack: one XOR with the original exe per mod and the hashes of the exes, loaders and
# original archives Impure knows, derived by tools/modpack/modpack.py and embedded in the DLL. Neither image is in it:
# only a byte a mod sets to zero reads as the original's, 15 B at the longest
# (research/notes/mod-manager-plan.md)
mods/patches.bin
